<title>UK: Sullom Voe berthings suspended due to high winds.</title>
<headline>Sullom Voe berthings suspended due to high winds.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Berthing at the Sullom Voe Brent Blend crude oil terminal in the Shetland Islands was suspended on Wednesday morning due to strong winds, but no tankers were waiting to load, a port official said.</p>
<p>&quot;Berting operations were suspended at 10 a.m. due to high speed winds but there are no vessels waiting to load,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>The next vessel due to load was not expected to arrive until Thursday.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7646</p>
</text>
